    "body": "Hello!  I made a comment on AVRO-2624 about how the ByteBuffer bug *shouldn't* be observable in our build.  \r\n\r\nIt looks like we see it here because the openjdk images fiddle with the `PATH` (instead of `update-java-alternatives` to provide the runtime).\r\n\r\nIn other words in the failing container, JDK 11 is used everywhere except when creating a new process without passing the `PATH` environment, and the failing python tether job is being run with JDK8.  I propose passing along the PATH so that the JDK of the user launching the test is also the JDK launching the tether job.",
